# Set the default behavior, in case people don't have core.autocrlf set, to handle line endings
# automatically for files detected as text and leave all files detected as binary untouched.
# eol=lf (not native) as the default: chezmoi renders every *.tmpl file's
# bytes verbatim into the target dotfile, so a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true silently CRLF-converting e.g. dot_zshrc.tmpl would
# produce a CRLF ~/.zshrc that zsh can't parse. Everything in this repo is
# consumed by Linux/macOS shells/tools, never by native Windows line-ending
# expectations, so there's no case where eol=lf is wrong here.
* text=auto eol=lf
